From 02e6846a79080db67b25d336a0d2504eea897262 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lech Piekarski <isilweo@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:02:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 34/34] arm64: dts: qcom: apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y: allow
 powering off the WLAN card

The QCA9379 on SDHC2 sometimes stops answering CMD52 when its driver
probes ("timed out while setting default block size", or later
"Could not init hif"), and then stays in that state across warm
reboots, because nothing removes its supply. On one unit this hit up to
half of the boots.

The vendor kernel powers the card down right after enumeration and
powers it up again, with a full SDIO reinitialization, when the WLAN
driver registers. Do the same here: the board can switch the card off
through its VDD supply (L11) and the reset line in wlan_pwrseq, so
advertise it with cap-power-off-card. The MMC core then runtime
suspends the card until ath10k_sdio probes and reinitializes it first.

This relies on the previous change keeping the I/O supply on. Without
it, resuming the card failed with -EBUSY in about half of the boots on
two other units. With both changes, 30 warm reboots each on the
affected unit and on one of those brought Wi-Fi up every time, with
Bluetooth set up normally, against 2 to 7 timeouts in 15 boots before.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-6.2-astra
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
index e3d3d64..019a874 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
@@ -571,6 +571,7 @@
 	vqmmc-supply = <&pm8953_l12>;
 
 	mmc-pwrseq = <&wlan_pwrseq>;
+	cap-power-off-card;
 	non-removable;
 	wakeup-source;
 	/* Some devices experience dropouts of the WiFi module at the default of
